<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Breitenfeld (1631)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1631">1631</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Breitenfeld · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Breitenfeld was fought in 1631 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leipzig">Leipzig</a> during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War. The Swedish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustavus-adolphus">Gustavus Adolphus</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> allies, decisively defeated the Catholic imperial army under Tilly. The victory demonstrated the effectiveness of Swedish military reforms and established the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a> as a major European power.</p></div>
